1
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:00,480
Thank you.

2
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:01,960
Wallet guy.

3
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:03,640
You live here?

4
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,000
What's wrong?

5
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:09,479
Please come out for a moment.

6
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:17,560
Hello.

7
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:19,680
Please come out for a moment.

8
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:24,920
Cao Jin, Criminal Investigation Brigade of Xinchun Public Security Bureau.

9
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,280
The guest in Room 305

10
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,480
died in the room early this morning.

11
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:29,800
What time did you

12
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,520
come back last night?

13
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,640
I was drunk last night.

14
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:37,240
I don't know what time it was.

15
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:41,840
When you came back,

16
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,079
did you see

17
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,380
anyone suspicious

18
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,970
or hear any strange noises?

19
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,320
No.

20
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,000
Nothing at all?

21
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:52,520
No.

22
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,160
Mr. Wang.

23
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,280
This is...

24
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,930
You know each other?

25
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:04,210
She brought me back yesterday.

26
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,120
Yes.

27
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,000
You are in Room 303?

28
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:09,640
Yes.

29
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,640
I stay in this room.

30
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:11,800
Then what time

31
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,560
did you check in?

32
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,400
Around 11:00 or 12:00.

33
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,360
11:00 or 12:00.

34
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:21,920
When you came back,

35
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,520
did you see anyone suspicious

36
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,240
or hear any strange noises?

37
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:28,760
No, we both drank yesterday.

38
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:29,800
After I sent him back,

39
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,200
I went back to my own room.

40
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:34,680
I see.

41
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:36,720
You two shouldn't

42
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,200
leave Xinchun for now.

43
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,240
We might need you

44
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:43,170
to cooperate with us for a detailed statement later.

45
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:50,970
This is my phone number.

46
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,079
If you remember anything later,

47
00:03:53,079 --> 00:03:54,210
contact me anytime.

48
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,079
Okay.

49
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:56,880
As for this floor,

50
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,320
we need to lock it down.

51
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:59,920
If you still want to stay here,

52
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,960
I'll tell the front desk

53
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,200
to change your floor.

54
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,050
Officer Cao.

55
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,880
Which 'Jin' is it?

56
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,490
The 'Jin' in 'Qianjin'.

57
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,200
What happened?

58
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:20,360
There was a murder in Room 305 next door.

59
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,560
Then we'd better listen to the police

60
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,020
and change rooms quickly.

61
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:25,520
Mr. Lin said

62
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:27,240
he wants to take a walk in the natural forest this afternoon.

63
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,170
Do you want to go?

64
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:29,680
Sure.

65
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:30,560
Okay.

66
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:31,880
Then pack up quickly.

67
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:33,940
I'll go home and get some clothes too.

68
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,970
Have you collected everything

69
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:53,140
found at the scene?

70
00:04:53,159 --> 00:04:53,890
Yes, we have.

71
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,640
The weirdest thing is

72
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,050
that red pine board.

73
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,120
What does it mean?

74
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,120
Does this hotel have surveillance?

75
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:06,200
No.

76
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:06,940
Then...

77
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:07,840
What about the statements?

78
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:08,640
They're done.

79
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,880
Not many people stayed here last night.

80
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,640
Do Wang Hong and Li...

81
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:14,240
Li Xuefei's

82
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,840
statements match?

83
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:16,640
Yes.

84
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:18,440
The receptionist saw them go in.

85
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,560
Li Xuefei booked a room last night

86
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:22,850
and asked to stay next to Wang Hong.

87
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,460
How about this.

88
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,760
You go up there again.

89
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,960
Ask for the detailed information

90
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,920
of Wang Hong and Li Xuefei

91
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,320
once more.

92
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,560
I just came down.

93
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:37,010
Are you going or not?

94
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,400
You're so lazy.

95
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:45,960
Teng Xiaohu.

96
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,610
What were you thinking,

97
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,159
ramming into Wang Hong's car on the street?

98
00:05:51,159 --> 00:05:52,560
The owner is Lin Shengli.

99
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,659
What are you doing?

100
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,040
Are you trying to make me look bad?

101
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:57,000
Lin Shengli is exactly who I wanted to ram.

102
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,240
If I didn't ram him,

103
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:00,300
they would have signed the contract.

104
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:03,160
Now all of Xinchun knows a Boss Wang has arrived.

105
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,290
I have to let him know

106
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,640
who we are.

107
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,040
Doing business requires proper methods.

108
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,520
You don't even know what they're about.

109
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:10,520
If you pull this stunt,

110
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:12,160
you'll scare the southerners away.

111
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,560
How are we supposed to do business then?

112
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,720
Dad, stay out of it.

113
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:15,920
I know what I'm doing.

114
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,480
As long as I get the contract signed for you in the end,

115
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,540
isn't that enough?

116
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,600
Are you just stubborn?

117
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,900
I'm your father. Would I harm you?

118
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,080
Besides,

119
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,120
do you think that old bastard Lin Shengli

120
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,720
will just swallow this loss?

121
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:28,240
I am stubborn.

122
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,440
My mom died early.

123
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,560
No one taught me or cared for me.

124
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,320
So what?

125
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,540
Why are you pulling this on me?

126
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:36,140
How about this.

127
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,920
You focus on the factory's production.

128
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:38,720
You don't need to worry about this anymore.

129
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,320
I'll keep an eye on it myself.

130
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:41,960
No, we don't even have orders.

131
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,200
What the hell are we producing?

132
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:44,440
Just give it a rest.

133
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,480
I can't give it a rest.

134
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,680
You give it a rest.

135
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,690
Where are you going?

136
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,800
Are you coming back for dinner tonight?

137
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,560
I had the kitchen

138
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,090
stew some big bones for you.

139
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:02,040
Hello?

140
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,120
Master Hu.

141
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,480
What's wrong?

142
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:07,880
What's wrong? Speak.

143
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,200
Liu Ming is gone.

144
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,240
What do you mean gone?

145
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:12,920
He's dead.

146
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,840
When did this happen?

147
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,320
Last night.

148
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,340
Still can't reach him?

149
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,120
It's so weird.

150
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,800
The samples have been sent over.

151
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,400
So why did he just disappear?

152
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,409
I don't know.

153
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,490
At the hotel I'm staying at,

154
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,960
someone died last night.

155
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:46,890
It was a bald guy.

156
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,360
Could it be that

157
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:50,159
the person you can't reach is...

158
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,050
I don't know either.

159
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:53,900
But there's one thing.

160
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,200
Li Xuefei

161
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,860
is staying next door to me.

162
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:57,880
Next door?

163
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,920
She was on the phone with Li Zhijun last night.

164
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,840
I won't be living at home for a while.

165
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:03,640
I think

166
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,170
her purpose isn't that simple.

167
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,040
I got it.

168
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,040
I'll look into it for you.

169
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:13,040
Take care of yourself.

170
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:13,480
Okay.

171
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,920
A piece of Korean pine board was found at the scene.

172
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,450
Want some instant noodles?

173
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:31,840
You have it.

174
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:32,970
Then I'll dig in.

175
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:45,840
Ma.

176
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:47,800
What do you think?

177
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:50,400
Why would the killer

178
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,840
not leave immediately after the murder,

179
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:55,240
but leave a piece of wood next to the victim?

180
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:56,640
What's the point?

181
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:59,040
I saw in movies

182
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:01,320
that serial killers

183
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,580
like to leave a mark or something.

184
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:05,880
You're already eating.

185
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:06,610
Officer Liu.

186
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,280
What serial killer?

187
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,980
The autopsy report is out.

188
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:10,970
It just came out.

189
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:13,400
The deceased is male, 42 years old.

190
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,160
Time of death

191
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:17,000
is preliminarily estimated to be between 1:00 AM and 3:00 AM.

192
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
The direct cause of death is a sharp object piercing the chest,

193
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,080
causing a ruptured heart and massive hemorrhage.

194
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:21,880
Sharp object?

195
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,460
What kind of sharp object?

196
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:25,010
Look at this.

197
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,770
The shape of this wound is very irregular.

198
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,020
It wasn't caused by

199
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:31,080
an ordinary fruit knife or dagger.

200
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,160
Those wounds are usually linear.

201
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,080
This wound is narrow,

202
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,040
but deep.

203
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,080
And the edges

204
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:39,080
show signs of tearing and crushing.

205
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,300
Sister Liu.

206
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:44,960
You mean the killer didn't use a conventional knife?

207
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:45,440
Right.

208
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,640
I believe

209
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,840
the murder weapon is likely a flat,

210
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,770
metal object with a certain width.

211
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:54,080
It's more like some kind of tool

212
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,960
or a part of something.

213
00:09:58,520 --> 00:09:59,000
Xiao Ma.

214
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:02,320
Detailed information on the deceased.

215
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,480
Liu Ming.

216
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:05,560
A local.

217
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:07,040
He did odd jobs here and there

218
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,700
and had no proper occupation.

219
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:11,300
What about his social relations?

220
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,200
He has a girlfriend

221
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,090
who lives east of the tree farm.

222
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:19,240
Did you check his household registration?

223
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,360
Both parents are dead.

224
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:22,090
He's the only one in the family.

225
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,050
Come with me,

226
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,120
Dr. Liu.

227
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,600
Nan, Gangzi,

228
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:27,800
come take a look at this autopsy report.

229
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:29,360
Watch out.

230
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:30,800
Good work.

231
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,260
[knocking]

232
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:53,160
Who is it so early in the morning?

233
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,210
What do you want?

234
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:57,080
We're from the Xinchun Public Security Bureau's Criminal Investigation Team.

235
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,720
We want to ask you a few questions.

236
00:10:58,720 --> 00:10:59,850
Do you know Liu Ming?

237
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:01,080
Yes. What's wrong?

238
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:02,640
Let me tell you,

239
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,240
we just live together.

240
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,280
I don't know anything about his business.

241
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:06,810
What's with your attitude?

242
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:09,140
Would we be here if Liu Ming were fine?

243
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,000
Didn't I tell you?

244
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:10,760
I don't know.

245
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:11,840
Miss,

246
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,260
it's just routine.

247
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,880
We'll leave after a few questions.

248
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,880
What does Liu Ming do for a living?

249
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,480
What can he do?

250
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,240
Just trading some scrap wood.

251
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,240
He made some money these past two years.

252
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,720
He used to be dirt poor.

253
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,080
Now he's so cocky,

254
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,200
always saying he's going to dump me.

255
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,480
I haven't wanted to be with him for a long time.

256
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,280
Liu Ming

257
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:29,650
died yesterday.

258
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:30,720
He's dead?

259
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,640
Think carefully.

260
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,280
Did he have any

261
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:36,880
unusual behavior recently?

262
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:38,600
How did he die?

263
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:41,040
He wasn't the type to cause trouble.

264
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,600
We're investigating that.

265
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,920
Until we find out,

266
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:44,920
you're also a suspect.

267
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:45,980
Cooperate with us.

268
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,770
He got a call the night before last.

269
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:50,930
He was very excited.

270
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,640
Then he left in a hurry.

271
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:54,200
He didn't come back all night.

272
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:56,320
I thought he went gambling again.

273
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:57,720
Officer,

274
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,800
I'm a good woman.

275
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,080
I didn't kill him.

276
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:02,850
Does he have any family?

277
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:03,840
No.

278
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,820
His family is gone. It's just him.

279
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:08,680
Do you know who he

280
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:09,440
was close to?

281
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:10,840
He was very peculiar.

282
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,040
He didn't have any friends.

283
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,720
He didn't tell me anything.

284
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:14,880
Officer,

285
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,240
I don't know anything.

286
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:17,920
I'm so scared my legs are weak.

287
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:19,280
Okay.

288
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,680
That's all for today.

289
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:22,560
We'll contact you if we need anything else.

290
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:24,320
Okay.

291
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,420
Let's look further ahead.

292
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:34,000
Officers.

293
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,140
Let me tell you something.

294
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,620
Come here. Let me tell you.

295
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,840
The guy in this room

296
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,160
is no good.

297
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:44,400
Every time he walks past

298
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,600
my house,

299
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,040
my dog

300
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,200
barks at him.

301
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:51,080
My Qiuqiu

302
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:51,920
is very well-behaved.

303
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:53,520
It never barks for no reason.

304
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:54,920
And let me tell you,

305
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,800
this guy used to carry logs years ago.

306
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,400
I don't know what happened these past two years,

307
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,680
but he suddenly got rich

308
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,080
and wears gold and silver.

309
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,080
I think this money

310
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,520
is dirty.

311
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:08,520
That's all I'm going to say.

312
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:09,160
I saw it.

313
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:09,880
Okay.

314
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:10,560
Okay.

315
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:11,280
Thank you.

316
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:13,680
Brother.

317
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,760
Could it be a vendetta?

318
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,050
Let's go back first.

319
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:22,200
What this lady said,

320
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:22,600
write it down.

321
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,660
I'll write it down.

322
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:26,040
Our Northeast

323
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:26,960
is vast and abundant.

324
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:27,560
This forest farm

325
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:29,220
has all kinds of tree species.

326
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:30,080
Well,

327
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:30,920
the coniferous species

328
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,480
include the Korean pine you want,

329
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,880
Mongolian pine, and fir.

330
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,200
The broad-leaved species

331
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,640
include Manchurian ash,

332
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:37,840
iron birch, and so on.

333
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,040
Mr. Lin,

334
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:43,800
no matter how hard the work is,

335
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,200
you still need to take care of your health.

336
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,240
It's a minor problem.

337
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,720
I cough when I catch a cold.

338
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,000
Mr. Wang.

339
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,690
I'm not much older than you.

340
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,120
Calling you Mr. Wang seems distant.

341
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,250
I'll call you Brother Wang from now on.

342
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,360
If you need anything in the future,

343
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,820
you can come to me anytime.

344
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,160
Well, when we go back,

345
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,440
I'll find you a new place to stay.

346
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,160
So you can live a little better.

347
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,440
No need to change places.

348
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,240
The hotel is quite comfortable.

349
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:05,720
Okay, it's up to you.

350
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:07,970
Let's look at this area.

351
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:09,960
There are a lot of trees here.

352
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:10,840
Including the one I mentioned earlier,

353
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,600
there's also iron birch over there.

354
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,480
As for iron birch,

355
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,940
we call it the king of wood.

356
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,330
Because it's very hard,

357
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,840
reaching 2,200 pounds per square inch.

358
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:20,960
Experts have tested it.

359
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:23,120
It's twice as hard as ordinary steel.

360
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,720
Besides making furniture,

361
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,480
it can also be used for aerospace parts.

362
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,760
You see that thin one,

363
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:29,080
it's called Manchurian ash.

364
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,440
It has strong corrosion resistance.

365
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,320
Besides making furniture,

366
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:32,080
it can also be used for floors,

367
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:32,600
and our doors and windows.

368
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,060
Mr. Lin.

369
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,570
I only want Korean pine.

370
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:39,760
Okay.

371
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,120
Today, I invited you to the forest farm

372
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:43,800
so you can have more choices.

373
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,160
Look at that white birch.

374
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,320
Our Shengli Furniture Factory uses this wood.

375
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:48,240
Its pattern is beautiful,

376
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,360
and it's very solid.

377
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,620
Any furniture made from it is beautiful.

378
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,200
Okay.

379
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,530
Let's go further ahead.

380
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,240
I think,

381
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,280
in about a week at most,

382
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,180
after another heavy snow,

383
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:02,010
we'll start logging this area.

384
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:04,840
Mr. Lin.

385
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,410
Is anyone living there?

386
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,530
That's a wooden cabin built by early loggers.

387
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,920
Someone should be living there.

388
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,500
Is it convenient to go?

389
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:17,720
I also want to see

390
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,450
what life is like in the forest.

391
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:21,120
It's convenient.

392
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,760
It's just an ordinary broken cabin.

393
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,760
There's really nothing much to see.

394
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,300
Does Miss Li want to go?

395
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:29,600
I'm fine with anything.

396
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:31,000
It's up to you and Mr. Lin.

397
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:32,570
We're already here anyway.

398
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:35,180
Then please lead the way, Mr. Lin.

399
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,940
Okay, let's go take a look.

400
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:38,940
Let's go, this way.

401
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,680
I haven't been here for a while.

402
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,140
This used to be all forest.

403
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:45,560
I only found out when we logged here.

404
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:46,680
Careful.

405
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:47,520
I'm fine.

406
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:47,920
Are you okay?

407
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:48,520
Thank you.

408
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:49,170
I'm fine.

409
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:52,930
Mr. Wang,

410
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:54,880
the further we go, the thicker the snow.

411
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:55,880
It's hard to walk.

412
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,920
How about we go back the way we came?

413
00:15:57,920 --> 00:15:58,520
Xuefei,

414
00:15:58,520 --> 00:15:59,520
don't push yourself.

415
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,960
I'll have Dajun take you down the mountain later.

416
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,960
Get some good rest.

417
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,360
I'll accompany Mr. Wang.

418
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,650
I'm really fine.

419
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,280
How about we just let it be today?

420
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,340
Let's continue walking in the woods.

421
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:10,880
Okay.

422
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:11,520
Miss Li,

423
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:12,880
what do you think?

424
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:16,760
Be careful with your high heels.
